  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection, guarantee and enforceability of rights: Peace and reconciliation from the territories</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is built based on the results and learnings generated in the project COL 223 and is seeking to contribute to peacebuilding and reconciliation in Colombia through the protection, enforceability and advocacy in favour of victims&apos; rights with a focus on access to justice, non-violent transformation of conflicts and knowledge management in 18 Colombian departments, 65 municipalities and the city of Bogot&#xe1; as Capital District. 
This will be achieved through three strategic objectives, including working with indigenous peoples, Afro-descendants and peasants farmers from rural communities, who are victims of violence, to defend and demand the right to territory, a healthy environment and a life free of violence, including gender-based violence, in an environment of legal, social and political guarantees free of threats and attacks for their work as human rights defenders in the territories; seeking to expand the guarantees for human rights defenders, social leaders, and/or the effective implementation of agreements and peace processes through comprehensive strategies for dialogue, negotiation and mediation; and victims of violence promoting alternatives to violent conflict through pedagogical and knowledge management processes that contribute to peace and reconciliation in schools and urban and rural communities.
This project is aligned with CINEP&#x2019;s new strategic institutional plan.</narrative>
  </description>
